@startuml
title Runtime Concurrency Model
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "Uvicorn process (one OS process)" as Proc {
  node "asyncio event loop (main thread)" as Loop {
    component "FastAPI handlers\nanalyze / jobs / settings / cookies" as Handlers
    component "EventBroker\nSSE listener queues" as Broker
    component "JobManager worker task 1..N\nN = configured concurrency" as Workers
    component "asyncio.Queue\nJobItem ids" as Queue
  }

  node "asyncio default ThreadPoolExecutor" as Pool {
    component "download thread\n_run_item_work (item A)" as ThreadA
    component "download thread\n_run_item_work (item B)" as ThreadB
  }

  database "SQLite (WAL)\ndata/app.sqlite3" as DB
}

component "yt-dlp Python API\nruns inside the download thread" as YTDLP
component "aria2c\noptional external process" as Aria2
component "ffmpeg\nexternal process" as FFmpeg

Handlers --> Queue : put item ids / enqueue
Handlers --> DB : request-scoped Session
Queue --> Workers : dequeue
Workers ..> ThreadA : asyncio.to_thread
Workers ..> ThreadB : asyncio.to_thread
ThreadA --> YTDLP
ThreadB --> YTDLP
YTDLP --> Aria2 : external_downloader\n(only when enabled)
YTDLP --> FFmpeg : merge video + audio
ThreadA --> DB : own Session, own commit
ThreadB --> DB : own Session, own commit
ThreadA ..> Broker : call_soon_threadsafe
ThreadB ..> Broker : call_soon_threadsafe
Broker --> Handlers : data: <json>\\n\\n

note right of Pool
One thread per in-flight video. The event loop
stays free for API and SSE: a worker never awaits
inside yt-dlp, it hands the whole call to a thread.
end note

note bottom of Loop
Locks and the loop hand-off:
* _item_claim_lock guards "refresh -> check queued
  -> set running -> commit" only, never the download.
* _cookie_import_lock is held briefly while a 403
  triggers a browser cookie re-import.
* Progress hooks run on the download thread, so they
  write through their own Session and publish with
  loop.call_soon_threadsafe.
end note
@enduml
